{"extract": "Pavel Sergeyevich Grachev (Russian: Па́вел Серге́евич Грачёв; 1 January 1948 – 23 September 2012), sometimes transliterated as Grachov or Grachyov, was a Russian Army General and the Defence Minister of the Russian Federation from 1992 to 1996; in 1988 he was awarded Hero of the Soviet Union gold star. As Defence Minister, Grachev gained notoriety because of his military incompetence displayed during the First Chechen War and the persistent allegations of involvement in enormous corruption scandals.", "links": [{"ns": 10, "title": "Template:Infobox officeholder", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Boris Yeltsin", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Communist Party of the Soviet Union", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Defence Minister of the Russian Federation", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "East Slavic naming customs", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "First Chechen War", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "General of the Army (Russia)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "General of the army (Russia)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Hero of the Soviet Union", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Krasnogorsk, Moscow Oblast", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Mikhail Kolesnikov (politician)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Military incompetence", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Minister of Defence (Russia)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Ministry of Defence (Russia)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Moscow Oblast", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Patronymic", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political corruption", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Russia", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Russian Airborne Forces", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Russian language", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Soviet Airborne Forces", "exists": true}, {"ns